Every other path in the method fails closed for an absent/unmapped id: extractId(null) returns null (lines 204-217), the map lookup yields no delegate, and the default UnmappedIdPasswordEncoder throws IllegalArgumentException for the null id (lines 227-240) — behavior also documented in the class Javadoc at lines 106-115. The early return instead converts "no password supplied" plus "no password stored" into a successful credential match. This type is what PasswordEncoderFactories.createDelegatingPasswordEncoder() returns (crypto/.../factory/PasswordEncoderFactories.java:61-76) and is the default encoder in the affected configuration lines.
